Codescape is licensed per directory. Copyright 2026 DreamLab AI.

  Path                       Licence                  Full text
  -------------------------  -----------------------  ------------------------------
  crates/codescape-model/    MIT OR Apache-2.0        LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE
  crates/codescape-collab/   MIT OR Apache-2.0        LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE
  crates/codescape-ingest/   AGPL-3.0-only            LICENSE-AGPL
  crates/codescape-layout/   AGPL-3.0-only            LICENSE-AGPL
  crates/codescape-server/   AGPL-3.0-only            LICENSE-AGPL
  client/                    AGPL-3.0-only            LICENSE-AGPL
  everything else            AGPL-3.0-only            LICENSE-AGPL

Each crate's Cargo.toml `license` field is authoritative for that crate. The
workspace default is AGPL-3.0-only; codescape-model and codescape-collab
override it with "MIT OR Apache-2.0" so they can be published and reused
without the copyleft.

Dependency rule: a permissively licensed crate never depends on an
AGPL-3.0-only crate. The two permissive crates depend only on each other
(collab on model) and on permissively licensed third-party crates.

Third-party code:
  graphicle (https://github.com/Graphicle-AI/graphicle), Apache-2.0, is a
  pinned git dependency of codescape-ingest. It is not vendored.
  visionclaw-wire (MIT OR Apache-2.0), published from VisionClaw, supplies
  the frozen 52-byte position record and its fixtures.

AGPL-3.0-only, section 13: if you run a modified codescape-server for users
over a network, you must offer them the corresponding source.
